(2508483, 346146, 16004, '<td valign="top">not having a toxic nuclear waste sign on the barrel feels like a slightly missed opportunity, but i still think this is a fun amusing image, and it actually conveys a sort of infectuous fun feeling too.  technically, i think the shot looks a little over cluttered, but i do like how clearly defined the shadows are, and the tones and colours are very pleasing also.  7.</td>', 'not having a toxic nuclear waste sign on the barrel feels like a slightly missed opportunity, but i still think this is a fun amusing image, and it actually conveys a sort of infectuous fun feeling too.  technically, i think the shot looks a little over cluttered, but i do like how clearly defined the shadows are, and the tones and colours are very pleasing also.  7.', '2006-06-12 04:38:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2508489, 345880, 60165, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, though shadows are not in focus so much ...</td>', 'Beautiful, though shadows are not in focus so much ...', '2006-06-12 04:44:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2508490, 344678, 16004, '<td valign="top">if you had cropped the picture more tightly to put the onus on the shapes cast by the petals shadow and the different tones of yellow because of the shadows and light, then i think it might appear to fit the challenge description better.  unfortunately, for me, it seems the shadow is purely a chance by-product of a (an admittedly well-taken) shot of a flower, and not so much a prominent element. also, i would suggest possibly scooting down a little more so your head is level with the flower; but that''s more personal preference and not a knock on your shot...  it is still very pretty, the colours are rich and bright, and the detail reasonably sharp...  piture gets 8, meeting challenge gets 4, so an average of 6.</td>', 'if you had cropped the picture more tightly to put the onus on the shapes cast by the petals shadow and the different tones of yellow because of the shadows and light, then i think it might appear to fit the challenge description better.  unfortunately, for me, it seems the shadow is purely a chance by-product of a (an admittedly well-taken) shot of a flower, and not so much a prominent element. also, i would suggest possibly scooting down a little more so your head is level with the flower; but that''s more personal preference and not a knock on your shot...  it is still very pretty, the colours are rich and bright, and the detail reasonably sharp...  piture gets 8, meeting challenge gets 4, so an average of 6.', '2006-06-12 04:45:13.000000', NULL, 1),
