(2521852, 346417, 51526, '<td valign="top">I would liked to seen the lable to see if you had great taste or not. Nice image, a bit more depth of feild to get your hand into focus would of beem nice. Good luck.</td>', 'I would liked to seen the lable to see if you had great taste or not. Nice image, a bit more depth of feild to get your hand into focus would of beem nice. Good luck.', '2006-06-16 02:49:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521941, 346096, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is a tremendous shot - you should put this on a stock library type site or something because it''s application in either advertisements or magazines is very fitting.  the colours, light, feeling, are all bright and happy, and it''s infectous.  my only grumble with it is that i don''t really believe it completely fits the point of the challenge, being that the shadow is a product of the shot, rather than a reason for it.  but as a photo, it''s wonderful.  the way you''ve captured the movement is very impressive. i even love the title. i gave this an 8.</td>', 'this is a tremendous shot - you should put this on a stock library type site or something because it''s application in either advertisements or magazines is very fitting.  the colours, light, feeling, are all bright and happy, and it''s infectous.  my only grumble with it is that i don''t really believe it completely fits the point of the challenge, being that the shadow is a product of the shot, rather than a reason for it.  but as a photo, it''s wonderful.  the way you''ve captured the movement is very impressive. i even love the title. i gave this an 8.', '2006-06-16 04:35:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521944, 346263, 16004, '<td valign="top">i actually like this one quite a lot.  i gave it an 8 - i like it''s subtlety, and the bright friendly colours...  would have also been a good entry in the recent compementary colours challenge.  i think it demonstrates great creativity, and you''ve found shadow in a place i would not have even thought of.  it looks so invitingly lovely!  and it would look great in a holiday brochure.  well done and good luck with this!</td>', 'i actually like this one quite a lot.  i gave it an 8 - i like it''s subtlety, and the bright friendly colours...  would have also been a good entry in the recent compementary colours challenge.  i think it demonstrates great creativity, and you''ve found shadow in a place i would not have even thought of.  it looks so invitingly lovely!  and it would look great in a holiday brochure.  well done and good luck with this!', '2006-06-16 04:46:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521947, 346058, 16004, '<td valign="top">great colours, lovely composition, this would look spiffing hanging on the wall in our kitchen.  i''m not sure the presence of the shadows actually adds very much to the already high quality of the shot, which is why i feel compelled to limit the score to an 8.  and stupid point, but i think the shape and pattern on the spoon kind of messes up the simplicity of the shot...  but that aside, i think it''s a great one.  the lighting on this is fabulous.</td>', 'great colours, lovely composition, this would look spiffing hanging on the wall in our kitchen.  i''m not sure the presence of the shadows actually adds very much to the already high quality of the shot, which is why i feel compelled to limit the score to an 8.  and stupid point, but i think the shape and pattern on the spoon kind of messes up the simplicity of the shot...  but that aside, i think it''s a great one.  the lighting on this is fabulous.', '2006-06-16 04:49:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521949, 346076, 16004, '<td valign="top">it''s a pity that this has now been so overdone; it''s obviously an homage to a great concept, but i don''t honestly think it adds anything new to the idea.  composition wise it also appears a little off-kilter, like it''s almost centered but isn''t quite.  i do find it interesting that it''s spanish(?) on one side and english on the other - it''s a good choice of pages.  but overall, didn''t really stir the soul - 4.</td>', 'it''s a pity that this has now been so overdone; it''s obviously an homage to a great concept, but i don''t honestly think it adds anything new to the idea.  composition wise it also appears a little off-kilter, like it''s almost centered but isn''t quite.  i do find it interesting that it''s spanish(?) on one side and english on the other - it''s a good choice of pages.  but overall, didn''t really stir the soul - 4.', '2006-06-16 04:54:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521953, 344409, 16004, '<td valign="top">this could look nice hanging on a wall in a fish and chip shop, but really, there is too much going on in this shot; it feels far too cluttered.  if you could crop out the boat on the far left, and use the burn tool liberally on the background to make the green boat stand out a bit more, i think that could work quite well.  or even do a 50% desturation on everything but the green boat??  and i''m sure a few people have mentioned reflections not being shadows, so i''ll drop it there.</td>', 'this could look nice hanging on a wall in a fish and chip shop, but really, there is too much going on in this shot; it feels far too cluttered.  if you could crop out the boat on the far left, and use the burn tool liberally on the background to make the green boat stand out a bit more, i think that could work quite well.  or even do a 50% desturation on everything but the green boat??  and i''m sure a few people have mentioned reflections not being shadows, so i''ll drop it there.', '2006-06-16 04:59:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521956, 346365, 16004, '<td valign="top">the best thing about this shot is the clever use of depth of field - i like how the water in the foreground is out of focus - it works with the image well and almost give the impression that it could be a small scale model.  i also like the moment you captured the boat; its tilt does convey a good sense of movement.  another good bit is the silhouette of the guy behind the black sail; it adds interest and makes you wonder what he''s up to.<br/> <br/>i feel it''s suffered though by the crop at the back - having the end chopped off makes it feel visually unbalanced.  the lighting on the hull could be improved with a bit of post process brightening.  and i hate to be one of those people, but it doesn''t really suit the challenge.  any shadows there are incidental, rather than integral, to the picture.</td>', 'the best thing about this shot is the clever use of depth of field - i like how the water in the foreground is out of focus - it works with the image well and almost give the impression that it could be a small scale model.  i also like the moment you captured the boat; its tilt does convey a good sense of movement.  another good bit is the silhouette of the guy behind the black sail; it adds interest and makes you wonder what he''s up to. i feel it''s suffered though by the crop at the back - having the end chopped off makes it feel visually unbalanced.  the lighting on the hull could be improved with a bit of post process brightening.  and i hate to be one of those people, but it doesn''t really suit the challenge.  any shadows there are incidental, rather than integral, to the picture.', '2006-06-16 05:10:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521959, 346449, 16004, '<td valign="top">i like this as a picture a lot - it''s very appealing.  it''s a mix of things, really; the lush greens, the shape the old rickety fence, the way it leads your eyes along the hill...  nice sky too.  i think the trees are a bit unfortunate in that they exist there, but save attacking them with an axe i guess there wasn''t much you could do about them, and at least you scooted down enough to minimise the impact in the background.  the shadow element doesn''t really hold enough interest, though, which given the challenge i thought should.  for me, this brought your score down from an 8 to a 7.  sorry</td>', 'i like this as a picture a lot - it''s very appealing.  it''s a mix of things, really; the lush greens, the shape the old rickety fence, the way it leads your eyes along the hill...  nice sky too.  i think the trees are a bit unfortunate in that they exist there, but save attacking them with an axe i guess there wasn''t much you could do about them, and at least you scooted down enough to minimise the impact in the background.  the shadow element doesn''t really hold enough interest, though, which given the challenge i thought should.  for me, this brought your score down from an 8 to a 7.  sorry', '2006-06-16 05:16:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521964, 345811, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is quite surreal, a bit bonkers, very striking, superbly moody, and very very likeable.  there is so much to love about this shot.  the colours of the tiles, the lighting, the choice of subject, the colours, tones and feel of the back wall.  the shadows aren''t quite obviously apparently integral to the shot, but they do convey some meaning the more you study it.  the only thing seriously letting you down is the light coming from (and presence of) the property in the background - just screws up the balance and i''m sitting here, cursing you for not moving / rotating round a little bit to get it out of the frame.  it''s one of those things that easy to miss when you''re actually taking a shot because your attention it naturally on the subject at hand.  like i said though, very striking image.  9.</td>', 'this is quite surreal, a bit bonkers, very striking, superbly moody, and very very likeable.  there is so much to love about this shot.  the colours of the tiles, the lighting, the choice of subject, the colours, tones and feel of the back wall.  the shadows aren''t quite obviously apparently integral to the shot, but they do convey some meaning the more you study it.  the only thing seriously letting you down is the light coming from (and presence of) the property in the background - just screws up the balance and i''m sitting here, cursing you for not moving / rotating round a little bit to get it out of the frame.  it''s one of those things that easy to miss when you''re actually taking a shot because your attention it naturally on the subject at hand.  like i said though, very striking image.  9.', '2006-06-16 05:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521972, 346503, 16004, '<td valign="top">composition is a little unusual in this one, as is the choice of tones...  not sure such warm orange / peach colours really works on something tha would normally be cold to touch.  the shallow depth of field adds interest, though i would have preferred the blurriness to start just behing the curve spine bit in the fork. i don''t normally refer the border, but here it''s so prominent (and distracting) i thought i should; something simpler, in a more complementary shade would probably work nicer.  it does meet the challenge, but overall it just lacks a certain pazzazz.  6.</td>', 'composition is a little unusual in this one, as is the choice of tones...  not sure such warm orange / peach colours really works on something tha would normally be cold to touch.  the shallow depth of field adds interest, though i would have preferred the blurriness to start just behing the curve spine bit in the fork. i don''t normally refer the border, but here it''s so prominent (and distracting) i thought i should; something simpler, in a more complementary shade would probably work nicer.  it does meet the challenge, but overall it just lacks a certain pazzazz.  6.', '2006-06-16 05:49:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2521995, 346343, 16004, '<td valign="top">one of the seven shots i gave a 10 this week. there is so much i love about this.  the optical illusion works brilliantly, and is very convincingly done - took a while to figure out how you did it.  it''s very funny (NASCAR and cooking?!). with the warm red background and the, erm, pleasantness of the shape cast by the shadow, rather sexy too.  lighting, composition, loads of other stuff i don''t even know about, is all perfect. it''s one of the best examples of challenge fitting i have seen. very well done!</td>', 'one of the seven shots i gave a 10 this week. there is so much i love about this.  the optical illusion works brilliantly, and is very convincingly done - took a while to figure out how you did it.  it''s very funny (NASCAR and cooking?!). with the warm red background and the, erm, pleasantness of the shape cast by the shadow, rather sexy too.  lighting, composition, loads of other stuff i don''t even know about, is all perfect. it''s one of the best examples of challenge fitting i have seen. very well done!', '2006-06-16 06:32:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522143, 345396, 16004, '<td valign="top">undoubtably a very pretty shot.  it''s sitting on the cusp about whether or not it meets the challenge; from the rays of light it''s clear shadows are being cast, it''s just you don''t get to see any of them (i personally don''t think silhuoettes are the same thing).  it is a fantastic sky though, and the detail of the trees outline is nicely captured.  i wonder if you tried shooting closer to the trees and with your back to the sun...  6.</td>', 'undoubtably a very pretty shot.  it''s sitting on the cusp about whether or not it meets the challenge; from the rays of light it''s clear shadows are being cast, it''s just you don''t get to see any of them (i personally don''t think silhuoettes are the same thing).  it is a fantastic sky though, and the detail of the trees outline is nicely captured.  i wonder if you tried shooting closer to the trees and with your back to the sun...  6.', '2006-06-16 09:42:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522149, 345373, 16004, '<td valign="top">can''t decide between a 6 or a 7 on this.  the sky is fab, though i don''t think it should really take up 75% of the frame as it does detract from the man and his dog.  i do like most of the post-editting - the tones, colours, and feel is really absorbing. for the most part i like the lighting (especially the single lamp) but i think it might be a bit heavy on the diffuse glow.  i also wonder why you didn''t take a minute to make the shot a bit less wonky, or even cropped closer to your subjects...  it has so much promise, it''s very creative, and even though he''s destressed, somehow amusingly over the top.  i''ll err on the side of caution and give it a 7.<br/> <br/>as a footnote i can''t stop wondering how it might be improved if you knocked out the dog by bopping him on the head, and then the man could be pining for the mutt - but that''s just my sick brain, so ignore it.</td>', 'can''t decide between a 6 or a 7 on this.  the sky is fab, though i don''t think it should really take up 75% of the frame as it does detract from the man and his dog.  i do like most of the post-editting - the tones, colours, and feel is really absorbing. for the most part i like the lighting (especially the single lamp) but i think it might be a bit heavy on the diffuse glow.  i also wonder why you didn''t take a minute to make the shot a bit less wonky, or even cropped closer to your subjects...  it has so much promise, it''s very creative, and even though he''s destressed, somehow amusingly over the top.  i''ll err on the side of caution and give it a 7. as a footnote i can''t stop wondering how it might be improved if you knocked out the dog by bopping him on the head, and then the man could be pining for the mutt - but that''s just my sick brain, so ignore it.', '2006-06-16 09:50:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522156, 345888, 16004, '<td valign="top">i''m bumping this up from a 2 to a 4 - in retropect i think i was a bit harsh.  i personally don''t think this is a shadow, more a silhuoette, but even though it slightly hurts my eyes looking at it, i am apreciating the drama in the shot more.  i like the undefined appearance of the sky, and i like the weirdness to the egdes of the birds wings.  it''s a bit mad, really.</td>', 'i''m bumping this up from a 2 to a 4 - in retropect i think i was a bit harsh.  i personally don''t think this is a shadow, more a silhuoette, but even though it slightly hurts my eyes looking at it, i am apreciating the drama in the shot more.  i like the undefined appearance of the sky, and i like the weirdness to the egdes of the birds wings.  it''s a bit mad, really.', '2006-06-16 09:55:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522168, 346061, 16004, '<td valign="top">this is weird and totally skewers my pre-conceived idea of what a shadow could, nay, should be.  and it totally works, in some weird mad bonkers inverted way - it''s amusing also because it looks like the wall was spray painted and the man was caught in the way...  yes, this is very creative.  i voted this with a 9.</td>', 'this is weird and totally skewers my pre-conceived idea of what a shadow could, nay, should be.  and it totally works, in some weird mad bonkers inverted way - it''s amusing also because it looks like the wall was spray painted and the man was caught in the way...  yes, this is very creative.  i voted this with a 9.', '2006-06-16 10:09:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522193, 346302, 34183, '<td valign="top">Excellent</td>', 'Excellent', '2006-06-16 10:22:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522202, 345886, 23098, '<td valign="top">Like your shot very much, colors, comp, hi key... nice job.</td>', 'Like your shot very much, colors, comp, hi key... nice job.', '2006-06-16 10:29:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522204, 346186, 23098, '<td valign="top">Super shot for the challenge.</td>', 'Super shot for the challenge.', '2006-06-16 10:29:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522210, 346264, 23098, '<td valign="top">Cleverly done arrangement! Makes me smile.</td>', 'Cleverly done arrangement! Makes me smile.', '2006-06-16 10:32:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522224, 346360, 23098, '<td valign="top">very nice image.</td>', 'very nice image.', '2006-06-16 10:38:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522241, 345325, 23098, '<td valign="top">Nice work.</td>', 'Nice work.', '2006-06-16 10:47:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522244, 346171, 23098, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shadow shot!</td>', 'Wonderful shadow shot!', '2006-06-16 10:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522246, 345387, 51538, '<td valign="top">Would have been tempted to clone out the left lower pole and gull and the upper right gull.  But then again, I like the gulls too.  The image is very crisp and clean.</td>', 'Would have been tempted to clone out the left lower pole and gull and the upper right gull.  But then again, I like the gulls too.  The image is very crisp and clean.', '2006-06-16 10:50:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522251, 346440, 51538, '<td valign="top">Elegant, simple and cleanly presented.  My only feeling and it is mine alone most like, is that the image is too clinically clean.</td>', 'Elegant, simple and cleanly presented.  My only feeling and it is mine alone most like, is that the image is too clinically clean.', '2006-06-16 10:51:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522255, 346059, 51538, '<td valign="top">I think the work you did in making this image is not quite reflected (no pun intended) in the result.  The result does not quite pop as much as, say, a simple black and white detailed shadow.  I think it is the white background that is taking away something from the impact.  Perhaps somehow framed in black it might have leaped out at me more.</td>', 'I think the work you did in making this image is not quite reflected (no pun intended) in the result.  The result does not quite pop as much as, say, a simple black and white detailed shadow.  I think it is the white background that is taking away something from the impact.  Perhaps somehow framed in black it might have leaped out at me more.', '2006-06-16 10:53:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522260, 346505, 23098, '<td valign="top">This is an eye-catcher. Nice one.</td>', 'This is an eye-catcher. Nice one.', '2006-06-16 10:54:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522261, 344962, 23098, '<td valign="top">love your shot.</td>', 'love your shot.', '2006-06-16 10:55:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522262, 346491, 51538, '<td valign="top">This has a lot of potential.  What comes to mind is shadow plays, a la those things they have in Bali.  I think this would have been better if there was a story - perhaps meaning two people interacting in some way - making the shadow.  The light at the top is a bit distracting too.</td>', 'This has a lot of potential.  What comes to mind is shadow plays, a la those things they have in Bali.  I think this would have been better if there was a story - perhaps meaning two people interacting in some way - making the shadow.  The light at the top is a bit distracting too.', '2006-06-16 10:55:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522264, 345680, 51538, '<td valign="top">Nice sky indeed.  The rock colour is lovely.  I think there is just a little bit too much rock and perhaps too much of the lower shadow as well.</td>', 'Nice sky indeed.  The rock colour is lovely.  I think there is just a little bit too much rock and perhaps too much of the lower shadow as well.', '2006-06-16 10:56:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522267, 346497, 51538, '<td valign="top">A good idea.  Entertaining.  But I think it could have been done better by using card cut-outs of, say, cactus in the foreground.  With some depth in the photo, by using cut-out layers, you could draw the viewer into the drama and picture.</td>', 'A good idea.  Entertaining.  But I think it could have been done better by using card cut-outs of, say, cactus in the foreground.  With some depth in the photo, by using cut-out layers, you could draw the viewer into the drama and picture.', '2006-06-16 10:57:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522274, 346500, 51538, '<td valign="top">The background is a nice colour and the tone is great.  My only suggestion would have been to have the model more central and compose the photo around a frace profile and the body frontal dancing with (important) the iPod cable clearly visible (which it is not in this photo).  The top of this photo is not contributing enough to the image.</td>', 'The background is a nice colour and the tone is great.  My only suggestion would have been to have the model more central and compose the photo around a frace profile and the body frontal dancing with (important) the iPod cable clearly visible (which it is not in this photo).  The top of this photo is not contributing enough to the image.', '2006-06-16 11:00:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522278, 344459, 51538, '<td valign="top">Easy to overlook this subtle rendition.  But it is really very good and something anyone from any culture can relate to.  The lighting is excellent.  The only flaw, IMO, is the strange face-profile-like shadow on the lower right of the wall where the blanket is.  Glad I reviewed this photo otherwise I might well have missed its quality.  Your quality control is very good.</td>', 'Easy to overlook this subtle rendition.  But it is really very good and something anyone from any culture can relate to.  The lighting is excellent.  The only flaw, IMO, is the strange face-profile-like shadow on the lower right of the wall where the blanket is.  Glad I reviewed this photo otherwise I might well have missed its quality.  Your quality control is very good.', '2006-06-16 11:02:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522280, 345956, 51538, '<td valign="top">It''s hard to resist taking photos of such pleasant sights and sensations.  But it is hard to frame them well and remove the unimportant elements.  I think you did pretty well.</td>', 'It''s hard to resist taking photos of such pleasant sights and sensations.  But it is hard to frame them well and remove the unimportant elements.  I think you did pretty well.', '2006-06-16 11:03:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522282, 346491, 23098, '<td valign="top">Good one! Colors, shadows, mood. Nice work.</td>', 'Good one! Colors, shadows, mood. Nice work.', '2006-06-16 11:05:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522283, 346220, 51538, '<td valign="top">That does look like a good photographic location.  Pity the architect did not make those collumns without the white mortar between the bricks.  But that is not your fault.  The family at the egde is very pleasingly composed - considering it is at such a distance, the people are very clearly defined.  It is a pity the people do not have some sort of shadow to show and it is a pity the sky is not one of those amazing white cloud in blue surreal ones you sometimes see.  With a little processing I think the sky could pop out a bit more.</td>', 'That does look like a good photographic location.  Pity the architect did not make those collumns without the white mortar between the bricks.  But that is not your fault.  The family at the egde is very pleasingly composed - considering it is at such a distance, the people are very clearly defined.  It is a pity the people do not have some sort of shadow to show and it is a pity the sky is not one of those amazing white cloud in blue surreal ones you sometimes see.  With a little processing I think the sky could pop out a bit more.', '2006-06-16 11:06:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522284, 344459, 23098, '<td valign="top">Definitely got the scary feeling across with this shot.</td>', 'Definitely got the scary feeling across with this shot.', '2006-06-16 11:06:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522286, 346477, 51538, '<td valign="top">The foot and show are a very nice combination with the stiped shadows.  But the rest of the body confuses it a little.  I wonder if bringing the other foot in and removing the body would have produced a more startlingly simple image?</td>', 'The foot and show are a very nice combination with the stiped shadows.  But the rest of the body confuses it a little.  I wonder if bringing the other foot in and removing the body would have produced a more startlingly simple image?', '2006-06-16 11:07:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522287, 346153, 23098, '<td valign="top">Cool lines and color.</td>', 'Cool lines and color.', '2006-06-16 11:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2522290, 346186, 51538, '<td valign="top">If only there was a girl passing by with motion blur.  This is nice and all but needs something.</td>', 'If only there was a girl passing by with motion blur.  This is nice and all but needs something.', '2006-06-16 11:08:19.000000', NULL, 1),
