(2528677, 346505, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by efren:</b></div><hr/><i> It is definately interesting! Captivating and somehow troublesome. would like to know how it was done. 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Here are the basic steps. The figures in parentheses after the Curves are (Input=Output) values for the control points on the Curves graph.<br/> <br/>-Printed out some question marks of various sizes and gray tones on clear film. Hung it up with some pants hangers, and used a standard swing-arm desk lamp to shine through it onto a whiteboard. <br/> <br/>-Handheld, macro mode. <br/>-Tungsten white balance <br/>-Cropped, slight rotation <br/>-Retouched a couple of small reflections near the top <br/>-RGB Curve to improve contrast (29=12) (67=78) <br/>-Individual Red, Green and Blue Curves to achieve the colorization<br/>--Red: (0=100) (25=5) (56=62) (74=100)<br/>--Green: (8=0) (69=72)<br/>--Blue: (0=100) (6=76) (74=98) (96=10)<br/>-Resized for DPC <br/>-USM at 88%/16 dia/TH = 0 <br/>-SaveAs JPEG at quality 7/10 = 125kb<br/> <br/>Resized original: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=349762" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/1031/thumb/349762.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/1031/thumb/349762.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/1031/thumb/349762.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Thanks everyone, for a great batch of comments!</td>', 'Originally posted by efren: It is definately interesting! Captivating and somehow troublesome. would like to know how it was done. 10  Here are the basic steps. The figures in parentheses after the Curves are (Input=Output) values for the control points on the Curves graph. -Printed out some question marks of various sizes and gray tones on clear film. Hung it up with some pants hangers, and used a standard swing-arm desk lamp to shine through it onto a whiteboard.  -Handheld, macro mode. -Tungsten white balance -Cropped, slight rotation -Retouched a couple of small reflections near the top -RGB Curve to improve contrast (29=12) (67=78) -Individual Red, Green and Blue Curves to achieve the colorization--Red: (0=100) (25=5) (56=62) (74=100)--Green: (8=0) (69=72)--Blue: (0=100) (6=76) (74=98) (96=10)-Resized for DPC -USM at 88%/16 dia/TH = 0 -SaveAs JPEG at quality 7/10 = 125kb Resized original:   Thanks everyone, for a great batch of comments!', '2006-06-19 13:40:01.000000', NULL, 0),
