(2568208, 344917, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Reading your intentions on the perception of this shot after the fact helps make the processing make sense. I dont think i got it during the challenge. Pretty funky colors and the shadow really stands out. I am sure it is not what voters were looking for though.</td>', 'Trading Post - Reading your intentions on the perception of this shot after the fact helps make the processing make sense. I dont think i got it during the challenge. Pretty funky colors and the shadow really stands out. I am sure it is not what voters were looking for though.', '2006-06-30 01:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574302, 345484, 37858, '<td valign="top">This shot is superb.  While I suspect some did not think the shadows were the focal point, and I guess they are right, I love the interplay of light and shadow and would have scored this an 8 had I not been on a trip and been unable to get online.  The colors are terrific too.  This would have worked exceptionally well in the green challenge as well. <br/> <br/>I like the lighting (duh) and I also like the placement of the walk.  While I might ordinarily use the rule of thirds to shift it to one side, in this instance I like your decision to put it down the middle.  It''s leading lines take my eye right into the shafts of light.  I also like the tonal quality of the greens.  You have a good range of green, from light leaves to detailed shadows.  Well done, I''d say.</td>', 'This shot is superb.  While I suspect some did not think the shadows were the focal point, and I guess they are right, I love the interplay of light and shadow and would have scored this an 8 had I not been on a trip and been unable to get online.  The colors are terrific too.  This would have worked exceptionally well in the green challenge as well.  I like the lighting (duh) and I also like the placement of the walk.  While I might ordinarily use the rule of thirds to shift it to one side, in this instance I like your decision to put it down the middle.  It''s leading lines take my eye right into the shafts of light.  I also like the tonal quality of the greens.  You have a good range of green, from light leaves to detailed shadows.  Well done, I''d say.', '2006-07-02 08:14:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574341, 346383, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading post.<br/> <br/>Excellent picture.  Wonderful abstract.  Super colors and lines.  Nice textures.  Obviously I am not the only one who thought so, given your high ranking.  Well done.  I have no idea how to improve on this image.  I would have scored this an 8 or 9 had I not been out of town.<br/></td>', 'Trading post. Excellent picture.  Wonderful abstract.  Super colors and lines.  Nice textures.  Obviously I am not the only one who thought so, given your high ranking.  Well done.  I have no idea how to improve on this image.  I would have scored this an 8 or 9 had I not been out of town.', '2006-07-02 08:45:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574368, 344917, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading Post<br/> <br/>I like the idea, but the colors are a bit over the top for me.  I was out fo town and couldn''t vote, but I would have scored it a 5 or 6.  I would have leaned toward a higher score if the colors weren''t so saturated (especially his hat, which has few details).</td>', 'Trading Post I like the idea, but the colors are a bit over the top for me.  I was out fo town and couldn''t vote, but I would have scored it a 5 or 6.  I would have leaned toward a higher score if the colors weren''t so saturated (especially his hat, which has few details).', '2006-07-02 09:12:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2574374, 346322, 37858, '<td valign="top">Trading post<br/> <br/>I am afraid this is going to sound like a broken record, but I also think that the focus is off and the shadows are not crisp.  I didn''t vote in this challenge because I was out of town, but I probably would have been in the 4 - 5 range.  I almost think this might have been better if the crop was not so close...to give more perspective at what I was looking at (beyond a shadow)...is it a window? ...a wood carving?  I can''t tell.  (o.k. I just saw the title.  Now I know what I am looking at.  All the same the picture didn''t really clue me in.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-02 08:24:53.</i></td>', 'Trading post I am afraid this is going to sound like a broken record, but I also think that the focus is off and the shadows are not crisp.  I didn''t vote in this challenge because I was out of town, but I probably would have been in the 4 - 5 range.  I almost think this might have been better if the crop was not so close...to give more perspective at what I was looking at (beyond a shadow)...is it a window? ...a wood carving?  I can''t tell.  (o.k. I just saw the title.  Now I know what I am looking at.  All the same the picture didn''t really clue me in.)', '2006-07-02 09:23:23.000000', '2006-07-02 09:24:53.000000', 0),
